# M5 status — 2026-10-06

M5 remains **in progress**. The latest [membership / IPPV pilot](pilot-membership-20261006/REPORT.md)
executes the full 48-call schedule on CA-GrQc and CA-CondMat: h=3,
k={5,10,15,20}, three repetitions, seed 20261003 and a 60-second limit.

| Graph | VF | Seven-patch IPPV | Paired output evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| CA-GrQc | 12/12 complete | 12/12 complete | 12/12 tie-aware matches; 6 strict |
| CA-CondMat | 12/12 timeout | 12/12 complete | No complete pairs in this campaign |

All 36 completed outputs pass separate structural checks and are stable across
repetitions. All 24 CA-GrQc outputs equal the earlier repaired-baseline campaign.
IPPV has lower median native time in all four completed CA-GrQc cells. The
previous single CA-CondMat VF completion in about 39 seconds is not repeated
within this campaign's 60-second limit; the source of timing variation is unknown.
Historical timings are kept separate. [Full time/RSS table](pilot-membership-20261006/aggregate/TABLE.md).

The experiment runner now retains native timeouts and continues the fixed
schedule, while still stopping for other failures or substantive disagreements.
133 Python tests pass. Saved-evidence verification checks 461 raw inventory
entries, and seven aggregate artifacts regenerate identically without solver
reruns. The campaign driver exits 1 because of its timeout outcomes; aggregation,
verification and regeneration exit 0. No C++ build/CTest/sanitizer rerun occurs.
Algorithm sources, four papers, the independent reference and historical records
are unchanged in this continuation.

Current baseline: IPPV commit `f61881d4752170c03585e4281f0c49d7ef14aa1e`, seven
recorded patches. [Reproduction repairs and correctness evidence](ippv/disagreement-20261005/REPORT.md)
remain distinct from performance results. IPPV's known zero-density omission
still limits full-domain comparison. DCLDS remains deferred; no techniques are imported.

P11.3's shared smoke gate is complete. P09.1, P11.1/P11.2, P12.1, P14.1 and
P15.1 have partial evidence; broader h/grid experiments, controlled ablations,
final comparison scope, clean-machine smoke and a reproducibility release remain
unfinished. Structural checks and cross-implementation agreement do not prove
maximality or the mathematical theorem. No general speedup or SOTA claim follows.

